ios-redfin bridge patch 0160: SWEET_FP16 -- half precision mode (default off = upstream rounding).
Base: metal2vulkan 720ef1ce + ios-redfin bridge patches 0001-0111, 0120, 0130-0137.
  SWEET_FP16=wide    half values stay in f32 and are never rounded back to half: lower/arith/narrow.rs
                     round / round_exact_below_normal / round_texel are the identity on half (no
                     FConvert f32->f16->f32 pair, no `x + -0.0` NoContraction barrier).
  SWEET_FP16=native  derive::Device::new inserts MetalHalfArithmetic, MetalHalfConversion and MetalHalfFma
                     into the driver deviations (unmeasured on Turnip: a relaxed-precision choice), so half
                     + - * emit 16-bit OpFAdd/OpFSub/Fma(a,b,-0), half fma the 16-bit Fma, and roundings the
                     conversion pair; the conversion barrier is dropped under either mode.
  Both cap a finite half code at 0x7C00 when stored (as native half rounding does). Off: byte-identical SPIR-V.
  The knob value is part of every cache key (env_vars::sweet_key_tag, as 0109), and `native` also changes
  the device profile fingerprint. Clear /var/local/m2v-cache/backboardd when switching.

